  "title": "Warsaw Ghetto Uprising",
  "summary": "On 19 April 1943, when German troops and police entered the Warsaw ghetto to deport its remaining Jews, about 700 young fighters of the Jewish Combat Organization and Jewish Military Union resisted. The Germans crushed the uprising by 16 May 1943. USHMM reports at least 7,000 Jews dying fighting or in hiding, and about 7,000 captured Jews deported to Treblinka.",
